# Artificial Intelligence – Assessment 1

## Candidate
Y.Roshitha (192424400

## Title
Analytical Problem Solving using Artificial Intelligence

## Objective
To understand and implement fundamental Artificial Intelligence concepts and search algorithms through practical problem-solving using Python.

## Software Used
Python 3.13

## Tools Used
Python IDLE

## Algorithms / AI Concepts Used
- Breadth First Search (BFS)
- Uniform Cost Search (UCS)
- Backtracking Search (bitmask-optimised)
- Model-based / Goal-based Intelligent Agents

## Problems Implemented
1. Water Jug Problem solved with a generic Breadth First Search (BFS) state-space solver
2. Mars Rover Agent Simulation (model-based, goal-driven agent)
3. 8-Queens Problem solved using bitmask-accelerated backtracking
4. OLA Cab Booking Agent (goal-based agent ranking cabs on ETA and driver rating)
5. Uniform Cost Search (UCS) for least-cost path finding with parent-pointer path reconstruction

## Repository Structure
```
├── Problem/       # Assessment Tool 1 question sheet (A1_Problem_AI.docx / .pdf)
├── Solution/       # Written conceptual solutions (A1_Solution_AI.docx / .pdf)
├── Report/         # Full report with explanations, code, and outputs (A1_Report_AI.docx / .pdf)
├── Source_Code/    # A1_SourceCode_AI.py – runnable Python source for all 5 problems
├── Output/         # A1_Output_AI.txt – captured console output (IDLE-style)
└── README.md
```

## How to Run
```
python Source_Code/A1_SourceCode_AI.py
```

## Result
Successfully implemented all five Artificial Intelligence programs using Python. The programs demonstrate the application of search algorithms, intelligent agents, and constraint satisfaction techniques to solve problems involving path finding, autonomous agent design, optimization, and goal-based decision-making.
